Falsifies `socket_contract::ephemeral::verification::an_allocation_never_moves_the_cursor_back_or_returns_a_held_port`.

The defect: the cursor takes the clock's position outright instead of the larger of the two,
so a clock behind the cursor moves it backwards and a port handed out before can come again.

Expected to fail: `assert!(ports.next >= start)`.

